####################################################################
# cardiac_arrest.dlog — HAND-AUTHORED. NOT GENERATED.
#
# TRIED as an on-demand query (like cat1a/cat1b/cat2a/cat2b) and REVERTED
# — kept as a STANDING rule. Real-corpus timing (patient 2826) got WORSE
# on-demand, not better: this check, unlike the alarm-scoped ones, is NOT
# bound to a specific arriving alarm (impliesClinicalEvent's subject is a
# PhysiologicalProcess) and runs UNCONDITIONALLY on every single alarm
# regardless of relevance — under a standing rule that's a cheap read
# against an incrementally-maintained answer; on demand it became a full,
# unscoped query recomputed from scratch on every alarm, which cost more
# overall than the standing-rule maintenance it was meant to avoid. See
# engine/replay_driver.py's ONDEMAND_RULE_NAMES comment for the full
# reasoning and the real-corpus evidence.
#
# One rule per file (split out of the former clinical_rules.dlog) so
# poc_entry.py can enable/disable each rule independently. RDFox Datalog
# port of FRAMEWORK/KNOWLEDGE_BASE/clinicalEvents.ttl's
# CardiacArrestCondition — see the migration plan
# (/Users/rzoodsm2/.claude/plans/we-re-going-for-the-magical-candy.md) for
# full background on the named-graph design this depends on.
#
# Every pattern carries its own independent graph term (`[?s,?p,?o] ?gN`,
# RDFox's documented syntax) EXCEPT the concluded tag, which ties to
# ?gRate specifically — hasRate is the fact that actually makes the
# condition true, so tying the concluded impliesClinicalEvent tag to
# ITS graph's lifecycle is what makes the tag disappear exactly when the
# alarm asserting the triggering VALUE ends. ?property/?process's
# isPropertyOf chain is left UNGRAPHED — a STANDING, concept-to-concept
# fact (inference.ttl), loaded once into the default graph.
####################################################################

@prefix mda:          <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#> .
@prefix metric:       <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric/> .
@prefix metricRate:   <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-rate/> .
@prefix clinicalEvent: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/clinical-event/> .

[?process, mda:impliesClinicalEvent, clinicalEvent:CardiacArrest] ?gRate :-
    [?metric, rdf:type, metric:HeartRate] ?gType,
    [?metric, mda:hasRate, metricRate:Absent] ?gRate,
    [?metric, mda:approximates, ?property] ?gApprox,
    [?property, mda:isPropertyOf, ?process] .

# VALIDATION — executed against real RDFox: positive (HeartRate + hasRate
# Absent) → 1. negative (HeartRate + hasRate Normal) → 0. Graph-lifecycle
# check: dropping ?gRate's graph (simulating the triggering alarm's own
# end) makes the tag disappear immediately.
